feterm (0.5.2-1~ppa1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release: adds a macOS port (Apple Silicon and Intel) with
    Cmd shortcuts. On Linux: the pty master is made non-blocking before
    fork, shortcut hints follow the configured keys, and [keys] accepts
    cmd/option as modifier names. No other change on Linux.

 -- Faheem Essack <faheem.essack@gmail.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:59:14 +0200

feterm (0.5.1-1~ppa1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Security release: harden against malicious SSH/SFTP servers and hostile
    terminal output. "Edit locally" no longer runs server-named executables,
    file:// links are restricted to local paths, ssh usernames are validated,
    sixel decoding is CPU-bounded, and OSC 7 / paste / parser handling is
    tightened. No user-visible behaviour change in normal use.

 -- Faheem Essack <faheem.essack@gmail.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:56:07 +0200

